  "question": {
    "text": "The foot of the normal from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> to a circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and a diameter of the circle has the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then the equation of the circle is&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
